'''Mōna''' is the innermost and larger of the two natural satellites of [[Basis]], the other being [[Aleya]].

It has active cryovolcanic activity, some surface frozen water, and a thin atmosphere composed mostly of oxygen and nitrogen which appear as an almost indistinguishable light halo around it. (Agus, 2024)

Orbits every 18 days. (Agus, 2024)

There are frozen water deposits in the surface and liquid water reservoirs subsurface accompanied by channels. As a result, extremophile unicellular organisms survive. Mōna maintains a stable atmosphere despite the low gravity. 
*Atmospheric Pressure: 50 microbars (0.00005 bars)
*Gas Percentages:
**Oxygen (O2): 0.05%
**Carbon Dioxide (CO2): 0.02%
**Argon (Ar): 0.1%
**Nitrogen (N2): 0.08%
*Atmospheric Density: 0.01 milligrams per cubic centimeter

